<title>SPAIN: GOLF-LEADING FINAL ROUND SCORES IN SPANISH OPEN.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING FINAL ROUND SCORES IN SPANISH OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading final round scores in</p>
<p>the Spanish Open golf tournament on Sunday (British unless</p>
<p>stated):</p>
<p>277 Mark James 67 68 73 69, Greg Norman (Australia) 69 70 68 70</p>
<p>James won in play-off at third extra hole.</p>
<p>278 Jarmo Sandelin (Sweden) 72 71 69 66, Eduardo Romero</p>
<p>(Argentina) 68 70 71 69</p>
<p>279 Jose Coceres (Argentina) 72 69 70 68, Jean-Louis Guepy</p>
<p>(France) 71 68 70 70, David Howell 70 71 67 71</p>
<p>280 Howard Clark 74 70 69 67, Fredrik Jacobson (Sweden)</p>
<p>73 71 69 67, Roger Chapman 70 67 74 69</p>
<p>281 Jose-Maria Olazabal (Spain) 69 71 74 67, Stephen Ames</p>
<p>(Trinidad) 68 75 70 68, Thomas Bjorn (Denmark) 68 69 72 72,</p>
<p>Peter Mitchell 70 69 69 73</p>
<p>282 Constantino Rocca (Italy) 70 70 71 71</p>
<p>283 Adam Hunter 70 71 73 69, Gary Clark 72 69 72 70,</p>
<p>Miguel Angel Jimenez (Spain) 68 74 71 70, Jamie Spence</p>
<p>73 70 70 70, Lee Westwood 69 68 73 73, Gary Emerson 67 72</p>
<p>70 74,</p>
<p>Ian Garbutt 69 70 70 74</p>
<p>284 Andrew Sherborne 72 71 71 70, Clinton Whitelaw (South</p>
<p>Africa)</p>
<p>69 70 71 74, David Carter 70 72 67 75</p>
<p>285 Dennis Edlund (Sweden) 73 68 75 69, Seve Ballesteros</p>
<p>(Spain)</p>
<p>70 73 73 69, Andrew Coltart 72 71 73 69, Mark Roe 70 71 73</p>
<p>71,</p>
<p>Greg Turner (New Zealand) 72 71 71 71, Stuart Cage 71 73 70</p>
<p>71,</p>
<p>Ignacio Garrido (Spain) 68 74 71 72, Silvio Grappasonni</p>
<p>(Italy)</p>
<p>71 72 70 72, Ross Drummond 73 69 70 73, Rolf Muntz</p>
<p>(Netherlands) 70 68 70 77</p>
